  "goodToKnow": "Der Liedermacher (die Liedermacherin) is a singer-songwriter, typically with guitar and political or poetic lyrics. The term became popular in the 1960s and 70s with artists like Reinhard Mey, Hannes Wader, Konstantin Wecker and Wolf Biermann. In 1976 the GDR stripped Biermann of his citizenship while he was on tour in the West, prompting a famous protest letter by East German writers. The plural is the same."
